Depending on the platform features used, we may process the following categories of data.
### Account data
- email address;
- user display name;
- registration date;
- interface language;
- profile settings;
- login history.
### Data related to rewards
- information about credited cashback;
- information about credited bonuses;
- use of bonuses;
- purchase confirmation history;
- participation history in platform programmes.
### Technical data
- IP address;
- browser type;
- device type;
- operating system version;
- browser language;
- visit dates and times;
- diagnostic information about platform operation.
### Location data
We may determine a user’s approximate location from their IP address.
This information may be used for:
- account security;
- fraud prevention;
- compliance with geographical restrictions of partner programmes;
- platform diagnostics.
We do not continuously track users’ geolocation.
### Research information
If a user voluntarily participates in research programmes, Cashback+ may receive information confirming participation that is necessary to credit the specified rewards.
The amount of information transferred depends on the terms of the relevant programme.

Personal data is used exclusively for purposes relating to the operation of the Cashback+ platform.
We may use data for:
- creating and maintaining an account;
- providing access to platform features;
- crediting cashback and bonuses;
- confirming eligibility for rewards;
- handling user requests;
- account security;
- fraud prevention;
- analysing and improving platform operation;
- complying with legal requirements;
- resolving disputes and considering submissions.
We do not sell users’ personal data to third parties.

To operate the platform, we may share a limited amount of data with the following categories of organisations:
- cloud infrastructure providers;
- security system providers;
- affiliate networks and programmes used to track purchases and credit rewards;
- payment providers;
- analytics services;
- research organisations, if the user participates in the relevant programme.
Data is shared only to the extent necessary to achieve the relevant purpose.

In some cases, personal data may be processed outside the United Kingdom.
If data is transferred to countries that do not provide a level of protection comparable to UK GDPR requirements, Cashback+ uses safeguards provided for by law, including:
- Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC);
- international data transfer agreements;
- other permitted safeguards.

We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to achieve the purposes of processing.
The retention period depends on the nature of the data, legal requirements and the need to protect the legitimate interests of the platform and users.
After account deletion, some data may be retained for up to one year or longer if necessary for:
- compliance with legal obligations;
- resolving disputes;
- fraud prevention;
- platform security;
- protecting the rights of users and Cashback+.
Once the relevant periods expire, the data is deleted or anonymised.

We apply reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal data.
These measures may include:
- HTTPS;
- data access controls;
- backups;
- security monitoring;
- auditing administrator actions;
- protection against unauthorised access.
Users’ passwords are not stored in plain text.
Passwords are processed and stored as cryptographic hashes using modern protection algorithms and cannot be restored to their original form.
Despite the measures taken, no system can guarantee absolute data security.

Under the UK GDPR, users have the right to:
- access their data;
- correct inaccurate data;
- have data deleted in circumstances provided for by law;
- restrict processing;
- object to processing;
- receive data in a portable format, where applicable;
- withdraw consent;
- lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.

Cashback+ uses cookies and similar technologies for:
- platform operation;
- security;
- saving user preferences;
- analysing service usage;
- confirming purchases;
- crediting cashback and rewards.
Further information is provided in the separate Cookie Policy.

Cashback+ is an information platform and consumer rewards programme.
Cashback, bonuses and other platform rewards:
- are not banking products;
- are not deposits;
- are not electronic money;
- are not investments;
- are not payment instruments.
Using the platform does not create banking, investment or other financial relationships between the user and Cashback+.

